    docs(SCHEDULER-ADMISSION): one query prints the ratio and the arm flag (CF-176 AC2/AC3)
    
    Re-reading CF-176's acceptance criteria after the first implementation commit surfaced two legs
    it still did not satisfy, so this commit finishes them rather than leaving the row half-closed.
    
    AC2: the paragraph's read-back query now prints the ratio beside the arm flag in one output
    (`case when cooldown_floor_s>0 then cooldown_ceiling_s/cooldown_floor_s end ratio, enabled,
    disabled_by`), so the ratio census and the enabled census cannot be reported from different
    queries again — which is exactly how the false family-wide claim survived the earlier correction.
    
    AC3: the sibling artifact that carried the same false value,
    docs/audits/code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-cf169-validator-claim.md:89 ("Every one of those rows is
    enabled=1"), now states the measured 16-of-17 and attributes the correction to CF-176. Its ratio
    numbers and refusal reasoning are untouched.
    
    Evidence file updated with both commands and their literal output, plus the two-commit
    disclosure: docs/audits/code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-CF-176.md.
    
    Gates at this commit: bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS (rc 0); bash scripts/boardctl
    validate -> RESULT: OK (3 pre-existing warnings).
    
